Z||000013||Songman||12-29-2000||09:04 AM||||I'm wondering if these scoops are mainly for looks or are they supposed to be functional. I know they can be used either way.<P>But more what I mean is, are they really any good or do they cause an airflow buildup under the engine cover? As I have heard and understood it, the vents in the back of a Fiero are for air to escape as it comes under the car. Now if you add a scoop up there pushing air downwards it seems to me that you are gonna raise the back of the car with all of that turbulence under there....<P>Am I over-thinking the situation?||||reg||1
Z||000014||Philphine||12-29-2000||10:24 AM||||never really considered that but just from driving over the past year i haven't noticed any difference on my temp guage (i am fighting with an unrelated temp prob. at least i think unrelated. it didn't start as soon as i put the scoop on). plus the real goal for me is to eventually have an actual ram air setup so that any air the scoop takes in would all be routed to the intake.<P>thats another reason i wish i could see what was done on the real indys.   <P>oops...just reread your post. the raising the car part i didn't think of at all. i've always thought of the vents just for engine cooling. but as i said, if i car route all incoming air to the intake it still shouldn't be a factor.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 12-29-2000).]||||reg||1
